00:47:44.640 --> 00:47:47.090
to go live.

00:47:47.090 --> 00:47:51.330
And now to speak a little about
discovery within the Assistant.

00:47:51.330 --> 00:47:54.120
How do people find
out about your action?

00:47:54.120 --> 00:47:58.050
Well, one is in the
Google Home app.

00:47:58.050 --> 00:48:00.330
The directory listing
is there so you

00:48:00.330 --> 00:48:04.680
can see users can browse
through and find things.

00:48:04.680 --> 00:48:08.220
And then there's also both
guarantied invocations

00:48:08.220 --> 00:48:09.630
and discovery pattern.

00:48:09.630 --> 00:48:11.820
So we think of
guaranteed invocation

00:48:11.820 --> 00:48:13.860
is much like your URL.

00:48:13.860 --> 00:48:15.621
You have a URL to your website.

00:48:15.621 --> 00:48:17.370
It's guaranteed if
people type in the URL,

00:48:17.370 --> 00:48:18.720
it goes to your website.

00:48:18.720 --> 00:48:20.730
So that's true of the
guaranteed invocations.

00:48:20.730 --> 00:48:23.090
There's a set of
phrases, for example,

00:48:23.090 --> 00:48:25.380
talk to, and then
your invocation name,

00:48:25.380 --> 00:48:28.080
will guarantee users get to you.

00:48:28.080 --> 00:48:31.650
And then there is
discovery patterns.

00:48:31.650 --> 00:48:35.940
And that's other triggers
that you can register for

00:48:35.940 --> 00:48:39.000
and other people can
register for them to.

00:48:39.000 --> 00:48:41.230
So then there's a
ranking problem,

00:48:41.230 --> 00:48:44.040
which Google's pretty
good at figuring out

00:48:44.040 --> 00:48:47.010
about who is going to win
that query for that user

00:48:47.010 --> 00:48:50.580
at that time based on a
whole host of signals.

00:48:50.580 --> 00:48:53.100
So you can register
for those, and they

00:48:53.100 --> 00:48:57.420
can be reasonably broad and
will still let you have those

00:48:57.420 --> 00:49:00.064
and occasionally
trigger for them.

